        {
          "title": "Modern JS Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Unpack, spread, collect",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Arrays unpack by ==position==",
                "Objects unpack by ==key==",
                "`...` is spread or rest, by where it sits"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const [a, b] = arr;",
                "const { x, y } = obj;",
                "const copy = [...arr, 5];",
                "const [first, ...others] = arr;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Spread",
                "Rest"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Direction",
                  "{blue:expands} out",
                  "{purple:collects} in"
                ],
                [
                  "Takes",
                  "iterable or object",
                  "remaining items"
                ],
                [
                  "Gives",
                  "separate elements",
                  "one array or object"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Safe access",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`?.` short-circuits to ==undefined== when the left is null or undefined",
                "Without it: **TypeError**",
                "`??` returns the right side only for ==null== or ==undefined=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const city = user?.address?.city ?? 'N/A';"
              ],
              "note": "undefined from ?. falls through to ??"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Template literals",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Backticks: `Hi ${name}`",
                "`${}` embeds ==any expression==",
                "Strings can span ==multiple lines=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`count ?? 10` keeps `0`; only ==null== and ==undefined== fall back."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Destructuring, Spread and Rest in Practice",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Destructuring, Spread and Rest in Practice",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Rename, Default, Nest",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`{ id: userId }` ==renames== the key to `userId`",
                "`role = 'guest'` applies only when the value is ==undefined==",
                "`null`, `0` and `''` keep their value, no default",
                "Nested `{ address: { city } }` {red:throws} if `address` is undefined"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const { id: userId, role = 'guest' } = user;",
                "const { address: { city } } = user;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rest and Spread",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Rest",
                "Spread"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Does",
                  "collects the remaining",
                  "expands into elements"
                ],
                [
                  "Position",
                  "==last== only",
                  "anywhere"
                ],
                [
                  "Example",
                  "`[first, ...others]`",
                  "`[...a, ...b]`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`const { a, ...remaining } = obj` collects the other keys",
                "`{ ...obj, k: 1 }` is a ==shallow copy==: nested objects are shared",
                "Later keys ==override== earlier ones in `{ ...a, ...b }`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Swap and Mistakes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`[a, b] = [b, a]` swaps two variables with no temp"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rest goes last",
              "text": "`[...others, last]` is a SyntaxError. Rest collects what is left, so nothing can follow it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Optional Chaining, ?? and Template Literals",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Optional Chaining, ?? and Template Literals",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Safe access and ??",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`obj?.prop`, `obj?.[key]`, `fn?.(args)`",
                "Broken link gives ==undefined==, no throw",
                "Guards only the part left of `?.`: `a?.b.c` throws if `b` is undefined"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "||",
                "??"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Replaces",
                  "every falsy value (0, '', false)",
                  "only null, undefined"
                ],
                [
                  "`count = 0`",
                  "gives 10",
                  "keeps 0"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`a ?? b || c` is a ==SyntaxError==; add parentheses",
                "`x ??= v` assigns only if `x` is null or undefined"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Template literals",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Untagged: `${}` values become strings, so objects print `[object Object]`",
                "Tagged: the tag gets the string parts, then the ==raw values== unconverted"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const tag = (s, v) => typeof v;",
                "console.log(tag`a${{}}b`);",
                "console.log(`a${{}}b`);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "object",
                "a[object Object]b"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why does `a?.b.c` throw?** `?.` guards only its left side.",
                "**Result of `0 ?? 10`?** 0; `||` gives 10.",
                "**Tagged vs plain `${}`?** The tag gets raw values; plain converts to strings."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Array Methods: map, filter, reduce",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Array Methods: map, filter, reduce",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What each one does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Returns",
                "Callback"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`map`",
                  "**new array**, same length",
                  "transforms each item"
                ],
                [
                  "`filter`",
                  "**new array**, maybe shorter",
                  "keeps items when ==truthy=="
                ],
                [
                  "`reduce`",
                  "**one value**",
                  "`(acc, item) => next`, `initial`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Always pass the ==initial value== to `reduce`",
                "`[].reduce(fn)` with no initial throws {red:TypeError}"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Callback forms and chaining",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Callback gets `(item, index, array)`",
                "{red:Gotcha}: `['1','2','3'].map(parseInt)` gives `[1, NaN, NaN]`",
                "`index` is passed to `parseInt` as the ==radix=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const total = orders",
                "  .filter(o => o.paid)",
                "  .map(o => o.total)",
                "  .reduce((s, t) => s + t, 0);"
              ],
              "note": "paid orders only, then totals, then sum"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mutation and mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Original array",
                "Methods"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{green:Untouched}",
                  "`map`, `filter`, `reduce`"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:Mutated}",
                  "`sort`, `push`, `splice`, `reverse`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`map` only for side effects: use `forEach`",
                "`reduce` callback that forgets to return `acc`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "reduce rule",
              "text": "Pass an ==initial value== and **return the accumulator** every step."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
